    {
      "id": "UgxVtpIgqRZrzAe58_14AaABAg",
      "author": "@leechumbley5440",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_kGbzuHsf8CGdiFeKVM3TKi9r4JmymtqTsx0WMjsLQvZuItYdhl3_7MMdXoz9-I9Xxg9g=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "I have a friend who comes from Iquitos. It was very interesting to see the city, neighboring communities and the wildlife. My friend is short and has a barrel chest, the sort of habitus typical of Peruvians who live in the high Andes. I theorise that his family must have moved to Iquitos in the recent past. My goodness, aren't the biggest fish huge! Fascinating that they must surface to draw air to supplement the oxygen in their bodies. The anacondas, the harpy eagles, the pink dolphins, the manatees - what extraordinary wildlife. Sad story of the exploitative abuse of the native peoples in harvesting latex from the rubber trees. Thank you for a video with many facets.",
      "likeCount": 6,
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T21:26:54Z",
